---
description: Cheapest flights worldwide, cash vs transferable credit-card points and airline miles, no paid flight APIs.
alwaysApply: false
---

When the user wants the cheapest flight between two places (or "anywhere"), a cash-vs-points
comparison, flexible-date or nearby-airport alternatives, or a price-watch on a route, load and
follow the repository's `SKILL.md` (Flight Points Optimiser). It is the source of truth.

Also load the matching `cards/<country>.yaml` when one exists. Never book, pay, or transfer
points without explicit go-ahead for that exact action. Never invent fares, award prices, or
ratios; cite a source for every number and label unverified figures.

Date flexibility is an explicit question, never a silent default. Before searching, ask whether
the dates are flexible and by how much: fixed, ±1 day, ±3 days, ±1 week, any time in a month,
or weekends only, and ask the return separately on a round trip. Search exact dates only if the
user says fixed. If you cannot ask, use ±3 days and say so. Scan that window and sample it when
it is wide. After the ranked table, always include an Alternative dates table (top 3–5 cheaper
depart/return pairs with absolute and percent savings, airline/stops, and the trade-off, or say
none were cheaper).
